1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--mad-libs-learning","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/mad-libs-learning","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/mad-libs-learning","sourceHash":"29dedb6117b4ff1093d0c744493c93b1f713c02e4009844e50b66a386e1fbc4c","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:53:21.662Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Mad-libs Learning","zh":"填空造句学习法"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Mad-libs learning is a technique where you learn a sentence template and practice swapping in different words to create variations. Named after the fill-in-the-blank word game, it builds flexible, production-ready language from a small number of patterns.","zh":"填空造句学习法是一种先学习句型模板，再通过替换不同词语来练习造句变化的技巧。它得名于一种填词游戏，能让你用少量句型构建灵活且可直接用于输出的语言能力。"}},{"id":"how-it-works","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How It Works","zh":"具体方法"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Learn a useful sentence template: \"Could you please ___?\"","zh":"学习一个实用的句型模板：“可以请你___吗？”"},{"en":"Practice filling in the blank with many different completions: \"help me,\" \"repeat that,\" \"show me the menu,\" \"close the door\"","zh":"用各种不同内容填入空白处练习：“帮帮我”“再说一遍”“给我看看菜单”“把门关上”"},{"en":"Once the template feels automatic, learn a new one","zh":"能够自然而然地使用这个模板后，再学习一个新模板"}]},{"id":"why-its-effective","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It's Effective","zh":"为什么有效"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This approach gives you maximum output capability from minimum memorization. A single template like \"I need ___\" can generate dozens of useful sentences.","zh":"这种方法能让你以最少的记忆量获得最大的输出能力。仅仅一个“我需要___”这样的模板，就能生成几十个实用句子。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"When you're preparing for specific real-life situations, mad-libs templates let you rapidly build a functional vocabulary for that context.","zh":"准备应对特定的现实场景时，填空造句模板能帮助你快速掌握在该语境中实用的词汇。"}},{"id":"when-its-useful","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When It's Useful","zh":"适用场景"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Mad-libs learning is introduced in Phase 4X (Situational Speaking) and is particularly valuable for:","zh":"填空造句学习法会在阶段 4X（情境口语）中引入，尤其适用于："}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Preparing for travel","zh":"为旅行做准备"},{"en":"Starting a job in the target language","zh":"开始一份需要使用目标语言的工作"},{"en":"Any situation where you need to be functional quickly in a specific context","zh":"任何需要你迅速具备应对某种特定场景的实用语言能力的情况"}]},{"id":"how-to-practice","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Practice","zh":"如何练习"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The best way to practice using these chunks and making phrases is by starting with chorusing clips, then adding in more pieces. Chunks can be found in phrase books, online, by asking tutors or an AI Chatbot.","zh":"练习使用这些语块和组织短语的最佳方式，是从跟读音频片段开始，然后逐步加入更多成分。你可以从短语手册、网络、老师或 AI 聊天机器人那里找到语块。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Make or download audio clips of native speakers saying the various things you want to practice. Then chorus them a bunch of times. Once you have them down, you can practice inserting various parts to fill in the blank.","zh":"自己制作或下载母语者说出各种练习内容的音频片段，然后反复跟读。熟练掌握后，就可以练习替换不同成分来填入空白处。"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"/roadmap/library/chorusing\">Chorusing</a>","zh":"<a href=\"/roadmap/library/chorusing\">跟读</a>"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
